cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  AI Security & Jailbreak Defence: an educational course teaching the
  model-and-prompt layer of LLM security through intentionally
  vulnerable models
message: >-
  If you use this course (in teaching, in your own AI-security training
  materials, or as a primary source in a research paper), please cite it
  using the metadata below.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Kereopa-Yorke
    given-names: Benjamin
repository-code: "https://github.com/Benjamin-KY/AISecurityModel"
url: "https://github.com/Benjamin-KY/AISecurityModel"
abstract: >-
  A 15-notebook educational course on AI security and jailbreak defence,
  built around a deliberately vulnerable LoRA-fine-tuned Qwen2.5-3B
  adapter (Zen0/Vulnerable-Edu-Qwen3B). The course follows a
  vulnerable-then-educate pattern: every notebook first demonstrates a
  working attack against the vulnerable model, then teaches the defence
  pattern that mitigates it. Coverage spans beginner attacks (DAN-style
  role-play, encoding bypass, crescendo, Skeleton Key), interpretability
  (attention visualisation, defence-by-introspection), automated
  red-teaming (notebook 7, the structural gold standard), prompt-
  engineering safety, real-time monitoring, multi-agent security,
  industry-specific compliance, fine-tuning robustness, multi-modal
  security, supply-chain security, and incident response and forensics.
  All compliance prose references Australian statutes (Privacy Act 1988,
  APRA CPS 234, ACSC Essential Eight, AI Ethics Principles) by name. The
  course ships with a working Gradio Space comparing vulnerable and
  defended modes, a 37 KB educator guide, fine-tuning scripts to
  regenerate the vulnerable adapter, and an OWASP-LLM-Top-10-mapped
  vulnerability taxonomy. The course code is Apache-2.0 and the course
  content is CC BY-SA 4.0.
keywords:
  - AI security
  - LLM safety
  - jailbreak defence
  - prompt injection
  - red-teaming
  - vulnerable-by-design model
  - LoRA fine-tuning
  - OWASP LLM Top 10
  - Australian compliance
  - APRA CPS 234
  - Privacy Act 1988
  - ACSC Essential Eight
  - AI ethics
  - security education
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-SA-4.0
version: 2.1.1
date-released: 2026-06-14
references:
  - type: software
    title: "harmless-harnesses"
    authors:
      - family-names: Kereopa-Yorke
        given-names: Benjamin
    repository-code: "https://github.com/Benjamin-KY/Harmless-Harnesses"
    abstract: >-
      Companion course teaching the structural-harness layer of LLM
      governance (policy router, source authority, prompt composer,
      output-contract enforcement, audit log + escalation FSM).
      Where this course teaches the model and prompt layer, harmless-
      harnesses teaches the scaffolding around the model.
